Ty: I chose “**Homelessness often develops through multiple interacting personal, social, economic, health, and structural challenges that accumulate over time rather than through one isolated cause.”**

Lacy: I agree. I thought this sentence worked best because it captures the main pattern participants described throughout the interviews. Unlike the other options, it does not reduce homelessness to only one factor such as housing costs, job loss, or family support. Instead, it reflects the idea that homelessness pathways are often layered and cumulative, with several forms of instability building on one another over time.

Lianne: Great. I added this study to our table.

